Qstn) : Given a string str & character ch, count the no. of times a character appears in the given string.
Ans): (in cpp)
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

class solution {
public:
    int countChar(string str, char ch) {
        //Write your code here...
        int freq = 0;
        for(int i = 0; i<=str.length(); i++){
            if(str[i]==ch){
                freq += 1;
            }
        }
        return freq;
    }
};
__________________________________________________________________________________________________________
Complexity Analysis
Time Complexity: O(n)
We traverse each character in the string once, making the time complexity linear, where n is the length of the string.

Space Complexity: O(1)
No additional space is used other than variables, resulting in constant space complexity.
